\subsubsection{Selecting the Target Batch}

A bare [[stop]] ends \enquote{what I am doing now}, and a hashless
[[edit]] (added later in this document) corrects it.  Both need the
same answer to \enquote{which batch is that?}.  If each computed the
answer separately, the two could drift apart, and an [[edit]] would
then correct a different session than the one a following [[stop]]
ends.  We therefore extract the selection into one method that both
call, making the agreement structural rather than coincidental.

The most recently started label identifies the batch.  Old session
files may predate batch records, so when the batch id is unknown we
degrade to that single label rather than failing---the same fallback
[[stop_labels]] has always used for such files.

The optional [[among]] restriction exists for window-scoped targeting
(\cref{track:window-batch-scope}): a caller may pass the set of batch
ids that qualify, and the walk simply skips more recent labels whose
batch is outside the set.  The restriction is a \emph{filter}, not an
alternative source of truth---membership and recency still come from
the session itself, so a stale id in the candidate set (its batch long
since stopped) matches no active label and costs nothing.  With
[[among=None]] the first iteration inspects the last label in
[[label_order]] and the behavior is exactly the unrestricted one.

<<active session class>>=
    def most_recent_batch_labels(
        self,
        among: set[int] | None = None,
    ) -> list[str]:
        """Return the most recent batch's still-active labels.

        The most recent batch is the one containing the most
        recently started label; with `among`, only batches whose
        id is in that set qualify.  Labels come back in batch
        order; the list is empty when no batch qualifies.
        """
        for label in reversed(self.label_order):
            _, _, batch_id = self.active_labels[label]
            if among is not None and batch_id not in among:
                continue
            if batch_id in self.batches:
                return [
                    l for l in self.batches[batch_id]
                    if l in self.active_labels
                ]
            return [label]
        return []

