De-duplication preserves first occurrence, matching the order the user
typed.  The effective start time is resolved here, while the old
labels still carry it: after the removal step below, a full
replacement would have no label left to read the batch's start from.

<<validate the batch edit>>=
if not old:
    raise ValueError("No such active batch")
deduped = list(dict.fromkeys(new_labels))
if not deduped:
    raise ValueError(
        "Cannot remove every label from the active session; "
        "use 'stop' instead"
    )
for label in deduped:
    if label not in old and label in self.active_labels:
        raise ValueError(
            f"Label '{label}' is already being tracked"
        )
effective_start = (
    start_time if start_time is not None
    else self.active_labels[old[0]][0]
)
order_snapshot = list(self.label_order)
last_old_member = max(old, key=order_snapshot.index)
@

The order snapshot and the batch's rearmost member are captured while
the old labels are still present---the anchor for the rebuild below
would be unrecoverable once a full replacement has dropped them.

<<drop corrected-away labels>>=
removed = [l for l in old if l not in deduped]
for label in removed:
    del self.active_labels[label]
@

Kept labels are rewritten even when nothing about them changes: batch
members share their start time by the [[start_labels]] invariant, so
writing [[effective_start]] back is the identity unless [[--at]] moved
it.

<<rewrite kept labels in place>>=
kept = [l for l in old if l in deduped]
for label in kept:
    _, old_notes, _ = self.active_labels[label]
    self.active_labels[label] = (
        effective_start,
        notes if notes is not None else old_notes,
        batch_id,
    )
@

Rebuilding [[label_order]] wholesale is simpler than in-place index
arithmetic: removed labels drop out, and added labels slot in right
after the batch's rearmost member's original position---whether that
member itself survived or was replaced---so the batch's recency
position is preserved exactly:

<<attach added labels to the batch>>=
added = [l for l in deduped if l not in old]
for label in added:
    self.active_labels[label] = (
        effective_start,
        notes if notes is not None else "",
        batch_id,
    )
new_order = []
for existing in order_snapshot:
    if existing not in removed:
        new_order.append(existing)
    if existing == last_old_member:
        new_order.extend(added)
self.label_order = new_order
