The [[show]], [[edit]] and [[rm]] commands all name their entry by a
hash prefix, which this helper turns back into the one entry it
identifies.  Prefix matching is deliberate: it is what lets the
abbreviated ids of [[track ls --id]] (\cref{sec:track-ls}) be typed
back, and it is why widening a displayed id never invalidates a
shorter prefix a user already copied.

The price of prefix matching is that a prefix can be ambiguous, and
the user cannot see why: the ids they were shown were unique in the
listing they were looking at.  The error therefore says how many
entries the prefix matches and what to do about it---a longer
prefix always exists, since the full hashes differ.

<<history entry helpers>>=
def resolve_tracking_entry(
    entries: list[TrackingEntry],
    hash_prefix: str,
) -> TrackingEntry:
    """Resolve a unique history entry from a hash prefix."""
    matches = [
        entry for entry in entries
        if entry.content_hash().startswith(hash_prefix)
    ]
    if not matches:
        raise ValueError(f"No tracking entry matches '{hash_prefix}'")
    if len(matches) > 1:
        raise ValueError(
            f"Tracking entry hash '{hash_prefix}' is ambiguous: "
            f"{len(matches)} entries match; "
            f"use a longer prefix"
        )
    return matches[0]
