A bare [[start]] resumes the last stopped labels, and the resume set
remembers its batch grouping (\cref{track:window-batch-scope}).
Passing the flat label list to [[start_tracking_labels]] would merge
every group into one fresh batch---precisely the structure loss the
grouped resume set exists to prevent.  This function instead restarts
one batch per group, inside a single
[[mutate_worker_tracking_state]] call so the whole resume is atomic,
and in list order, which restores the groups' relative recency (new
batch ids grow monotonically).  It returns the same
[[(started, already_tracking, discarded)]] triple as
[[start_tracking_labels]] so the [[start]] command's reporting code
serves both paths.

<<session management>>=
