A group's labels may have been restarted individually since the stop;
[[start_labels]] skips active labels, and a group whose every label is
already running contributes no new batch.  The freshly started labels
share one batch id by the [[start_labels]] invariant, so reading it
off the first suffices.

<<restart each stopped group as its own batch>>=
for group in list(session.last_stopped):
    labels = list(group["labels"])
    started = session.start_labels(labels, start_time)
    if not started:
        already_tracking.extend(labels)
        continue
    started_labels.extend(started)
    already_tracking.extend(
        label for label in labels
        if label not in started
    )
    resumed_groups.append({
        "labels": started,
        "batch": session.active_labels[started[0]][2],
        "window": group.get("window"),
        "server_key": group.get("server_key"),
    })
@

Re-registration is what makes the round trip complete: a window-tagged
group returns to \emph{its} window's file, with its new batch id, even
when the [[start]] was typed somewhere else.  The existence check is
the \enquote{window still exists} test, and it deliberately accepts
the empty tracked marker---stopping everything in a window keeps the
file precisely so that this resume re-attaches the labels instead of
degrading them to globals.  A group whose window is gone (file
deleted, other server, never tagged) falls back to today's behavior:
register into whatever pane/window context the command runs in.
Window-tagged groups skip the current pane file on purpose---they
belong to their window, not to the pane the user happened to type in.

<<register resumed groups into their windows>>=
for group in resumed_groups:
    window_id = group["window"]
    server_key = group["server_key"]
    if (
        window_id
        and server_key
        and read_window_labels(
            window_id, resolved_who, server_key,
        ) is not None
    ):
        add_window_labels(
            window_id, resolved_who, server_key,
            group["labels"],
            batches={
                label: group["batch"]
                for label in group["labels"]
            },
        )
    else:
        _register_tmux_context_labels_unlocked(
            group["labels"], resolved_who,
            session=session,
        )
