The window auto-suspend transition resumes a window the same way a
bare [[start]] resumes a stop: it must not flatten.  Suspending a
window stops its labels but leaves them (and their batch ids) in the
window file; restarting them in one call would merge the window's
batches into one, which is why, historically, a bare [[stop]] after
switching windows stopped \emph{all} the window's labels instead of
the latest batch.  Here the file's per-label batch ids are the
grouping key: labels sharing an old id restart together (one new batch
per group; ids without a record---legacy files---form one group), and
the file is refreshed with the new ids afterwards, under the same
locks, so the next suspend groups correctly again.  The refresh reads
the ids off the updated session rather than the start calls: a label
that was already running elsewhere keeps its current batch, and the
file should say so.

<<session management>>=
def restart_window_batches(
    *,
    who: str = None,
    window_id: str,
    tmux_server_key: str,
    label_batches: dict,
    start_time: datetime.datetime = None,
):
    """Restart a window's labels, one batch per file group."""
    if start_time is None:
        start_time = datetime.datetime.now()
    resolved_who = (
        who if who is not None
        else default_username
    )
    groups = {}
    for label, batch_id in label_batches.items():
        groups.setdefault(batch_id, []).append(label)

    def update(session, history_entries):
        for group_labels in groups.values():
            session.start_labels(
                group_labels, start_time,
            )
        return session, history_entries

    def refresh_window_file(session, history_entries):
        update_window_label_batches(
            window_id, resolved_who, tmux_server_key,
            {
                label: session.active_labels[label][2]
                for label in label_batches
                if label in session.active_labels
            },
        )

    mutate_worker_tracking_state(
        update, who,
        post_update=refresh_window_file,
    )
@

