Two of these options change meaning with the mode, and the help texts
above say so.  [[--who]] follows the command's target: on a historical
entry it rewrites the stored worker field, while on the active session
it selects \emph{whose} session to correct, matching every other
active-session command ([[start]], [[stop]], [[switch]], [[notes]]).
[[--description]] maps onto the session's notes, because notes are
what [[stop_labels]] turns into the entry's description---editing them
now \emph{is} editing the future description.

[[edit]] also needs its own hash argument.  [[show]] and [[rm]] keep
the shared required [[entry_hash_arg]]: for them a missing target is
meaningless.  For [[edit]] we follow the [[labels_switch_arg]]
precedent and omit the required marker so the parameter can default to
[[None]]:

<<argument and option definitions>>=
edit_entry_hash_arg = typer.Argument(
    help="Tracking entry hash prefix; omit to edit "
    "the currently tracking session",
    autocompletion=complete_entry_hashes)
@

Two further options exist only for the hashless mode.
[[--containing]] selects the target batch by one of its labels instead
of by recency: a scripted caller (the mutt-nytid integration in
[[dbosk/edumail]] is the concrete consumer, issue~\#472) knows
\emph{which} labels it started and must not have its correction land
on whatever batch happens to be newest---tracking started meanwhile
from another terminal would silently steal the default target.
[[--discard]] confirms an edit that removes \emph{every} label of the
batch: the batch is dropped without a history entry.  It is a
deliberate extra flag rather than implicit behavior so an interactive
typo cannot silently erase tracked time.

<<argument and option definitions>>=
containing_opt = typer.Option(
    "--containing",
    help="Target the active batch containing this label "
         "instead of the most recent one (no-hash mode)",
    autocompletion=complete_active_labels)
discard_opt = typer.Option(
    "--discard",
    help="Allow removing every label of the batch; it is "
         "dropped without a history entry (no-hash mode)")
